<rml>
<head>
	<title>Main Frame Background</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="main_frame_bg.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="main_frame_bg">
	<!-- Loaded into RmlUiRuntime's background context (GetBackgroundContext()), not the "main"
	     one main_frame.rml uses -- CNewUIMainFrameWindow::RenderLeftFrame()'s own header comment
	     explains why: this panel must sit BEHIND the legacy 3D-composited item/skill icons, which
	     the "main" context's single fixed render pass can never do. root_x/root_y/root_scale
	     mirror main_frame.rml's own #bars left/top/scale exactly (same C++ source values,
	     CNewUIMainFrameWindow::SyncRmlModel()); left_offset_x/center_offset_x are the same
	     item-hotkey/skill-hotkey anchor deltas #bars's own children read indirectly via that
	     shared transform. Reference-space (152/214/424/429/41 etc.) coordinates below are
	     identical to the legacy RenderColorQuadARGB() calls this panel replaces
	     (RenderLeftFrame()/RenderCenterFrame()) -- kept in sync by inspection, not by a shared
	     constant, same as every other reference-space RmlUi/C++ pair in this file's sibling
	     main_frame.rml. -->
	<div id="bg_root" data-style-left="root_x + 'px'" data-style-top="root_y + 'px'"
	     data-style-transform="'scale(' + root_scale + ')'">
		<div id="bg_left" data-style-left="left_offset_x + 'px'"></div>
		<div id="bg_center" data-style-left="center_offset_x + 214 + 'px'"></div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
